course: dictionary
lesson: 5974
title: Many meanings of may
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «May» is a small word with several jobs. Often it shows that something is allowed: «You may go out now.» The person speaking is giving permission.
explain: It can also show that something is possible, not certain: «It may rain later.» Nobody knows for sure, but rain is a real chance. Check the sentence: «may» usually sits in front of a verb, like go, rain or nest.
explain: Capital M often means the month or a name, as in «May is my birthday month». A small m beside a verb usually means allowed or possible. Read the words around it, and ask which meaning fits.
fact: «May» means something is allowed: «You may go out.»
fact: «May» means something is possible: «It may rain.» The softer word «might» means the same kind of thing but is less likely: «It might rain.»
fact: «May not» means it is forbidden or not allowed: «Candidates may not use a phone.» It can also mean something is not very likely: «People online may not be who they say they are.»
fact: «May» is the fifth month of the year, with 31 days.
fact: May is also a tree, the hawthorn, with white spring flowers.
exercise: «You may borrow two books from the library.» What does may mean here? | It is certain to happen | It is the name of a month | *It is allowed | It is a tree with white flowers
exercise: «It may rain later, so take a coat.» What does may mean here? | It is the fifth month of the year | *It is possible | It is a polite question | It is forbidden
exercise: Which month comes after April and has 31 days? | *May | February | March | June
test: «May I come in?» What kind of question is this? | A rule about a calculator | Something certain to happen | A tree with white flowers | *A polite request for permission
test: «May you have a long life.» What is this sentence doing? | *Making a formal wish | Naming a month | Saying something is possible | Giving a rule
exam: «Candidates may not use a calculator in this paper.» What does may not mean? | *It is not permitted by the rules | It is possible they will use one | It is a tree with white flowers | It is a month of 31 days
